# Every env file, not just the two we happen to have. .env.prod holds the remote
# project's keys and .env.local the local stack's; a third one arrives the moment
# somebody tries something. If an example file is ever wanted, it needs an
# explicit `!.env.example` below — this pattern would swallow it.
.env*
